    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <h1><a name=""></a></h1>

<p><b>Bug Type:</b> Functional / Combat / Hitbox Collision</p>

<p><b>Priority:</b> High</p>

<p><b>Preconditions:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Game is running and the player has entered the Orc Rider boss room.</li>
	<li>The selected character is Yugi.</li>
	<li>The Orc Rider boss is active and able to perform attacks.</li>
	<li>The player has sufficient HP and armor to survive an attack.</li>
	<li>No invincibility frames (I-Frames), guard effects, or temporary damage immunity are active.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Start the game and select Yugi.</li>
	<li>Enter the Orc Rider boss room.</li>
	<li>Approach the boss and position Yugi directly below it, close enough to be within the intended attack range.</li>
	<li>Remain in this position while the boss performs its normal attacks.</li>
	<li>Wait for the boss to activate its spinning attack, indicated by a red circular warning area.</li>
	<li>Stay inside the visually indicated attack area until the attack animation finishes.</li>
	<li>Observe whether the player takes damage.</li>
	<li>Continue attacking the boss from this position and observe its behavior.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The Orc Rider should be able to damage the player when the player is within the intended attack range, regardless of whether the player approaches from above, below, left, or right.</li>
	<li>The attack hitbox should accurately match the attack animation and warning area.</li>
	<li>If the player is inside the spinning attack's damage area when the attack connects, the player's armor or HP should decrease accordingly, unless a valid defensive effect is active.</li>
	<li>The player should not be able to exploit a position directly below the boss to avoid attacks that should otherwise hit.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>When Yugi stands directly below the Orc Rider, the boss continues performing attack animations.</li>
	<li>The boss displays its red circular warning area and executes the spinning attack.</li>
	<li>Despite remaining in the visually indicated attack area, the player does not receive the expected damage.</li>
	<li>The player can continue attacking the boss from this position without being hit by the observed attacks.</li>
	<li>This creates a potential safe spot that allows the player to defeat the boss without taking damage.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Test Case Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><b>FAIL</b></li>
	<li><b>Related Test Cases:</b> TC-BS-07 (boss chasing and attacking behavior); TC-BS-08 and TC-BS-09 should also be reviewed for potential attack coverage.</li>
	<li><b>Regression Testing:</b> Required after the issue is fixed.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Notes:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The issue appears to be related to a mismatch between the Orc Rider's attack hitboxes and the visible attack animations.</li>
	<li>Source code inspection shows that the boss uses three attack collision shapes (<tt>Shape1</tt>, <tt>Shape2</tt>, and <tt>Shape3</tt>) to detect hits.</li>
	<li>In <tt>orc_rider.tscn</tt>, these collision shapes are positioned above or to the side of the boss's origin. This may leave insufficient hitbox coverage directly below the boss.</li>
	<li>The spinning attack displays a circular warning area with a radius of 65 pixels, but its actual damage hitbox uses a rectangular collision shape. This may cause inconsistencies between the warning indicator and the effective damage area.</li>
	<li>Verify whether the hitboxes correctly cover the player's position below the boss.</li>
	<li>Compare the collision shapes with their corresponding attack animations.</li>
	<li>Check whether the issue affects only the spinning attack or also the boss's normal attacks and charge attack.</li>
	<li>Repeat the test with other playable characters to determine whether the issue is specific to Yugi.</li>
	<li>Verify that no I-Frames, guard effects, or damage immunity are active during testing.</li>
	<li>Check whether the issue occurs in different boss phases and at different distances.</li>
	<li>This issue may be related to the previously reported Orc Rider AI exploit (TC-BS-07), but it should be investigated separately because the boss is still performing attacks in this scenario.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Relevant Source Files:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><tt>Scene/Enemies/Boss/Orc Rider/orc_rider.gd</tt></li>
	<li><tt>Scene/Enemies/Boss/Orc Rider/orc_rider.tscn</tt></li>
</ul>


<p><b>Attachment:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><tt>Screen Recording 2026-11-18 215251.mp4</tt></li>
</ul>


<p><b>Status:</b> To Do</p>
